                  "to": 134.775,
                  "from": 122.775,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2887305,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "By the mid fifteen hundreds, coffee bushes were being cultivated in the Yemen, and for the next hundred years, this region produced most of the coffee drunk in Africa and the Arab world. What's particularly interesting about coffee is its effect on social life. It was rarely drunk at home, but instead people went to coffee houses to drink it. These people, usually men, would meet to drink coffee and chat about issues of the day. But at the time, this chance to share ideas and opinions was seen as something that was potentially dangerous.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2887306,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "By the mid fifteen hundreds, coffee bushes were being cultivated in the Yemen, and for the next hundred years, this region produced most of the coffee drunk in Africa and the Arab world.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 149.17,
                  "from": 136.69,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2887340,
                "level": 2,
